          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.37,
            0.11,
            0.629,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.153,
            0.885,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "sequence",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is an ordered list of numbers. Each number in the list is called a term."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.203,
            0.886,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "general formula",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or rule for a sequence is a rule that can be used to generate each term. An "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "explicit formula",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a rule that uses the term’s position number, n, to calculate the term’s value."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.273,
            0.885,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "recursive formula",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a rule that gives the value of a given term using the values of previous terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.322,
            0.885,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "triangular number sequence",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is given by 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, … Each term is the sum of the natural numbers up to the position of that term. The "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term is given by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t_{n}=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which is also the formula for the sum of the first n natural numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.426,
            0.886,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "arithmetic progression",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (AP) is a list of numbers in which each term after the first term is obtained by adding a fixed number d to the previous term. The fixed number d is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "common difference",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.516,
            0.886,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term of an AP is given by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t_{n}=\\bar{a}+(n-1)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " d, where a is the first term and d is the common difference. The general form of an AP is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a,a+d,a+2d,a+3d,...,a+(n-1)c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.586,
            0.886,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "geometric progression",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (GP) is a list of numbers in which each term after the first term is obtained by multiplying the previous term by a fixed number. This constant factor r is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "common ratio",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.676,
            0.885,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• The "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term of a GP is given by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "t _ { _ { n } } = a r ^ { { _ { n - 1 } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the first term and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\boldsymbol { ^ { * } r ^ { * } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the common ratio. The general form of a GP is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a , a r , a r ^ { 2 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a r ^ { 3 } , . . . , \\bar { a } \\bar { r } ^ { \\bar { n } - 1 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.746,
            0.886,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Many attributes of fractals, such as the Sierpiński triangle and the Sierpiński square carpet, lead to geometric progressions."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
